From a3ed0c7faf326e8004a01e55b22cd917dec4754f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:17:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/45] dt-bindings: display/msm/gpu: add the Adreno 830
 (0x44050000)

The Adreno 830 GPU of SM8750 uses the chip-id compatible
qcom,adreno-44050000. It already matches the generic chip-id pattern.
Like the other A7xx/A8xx parts its clocks live in the GMU node, so add
it to that list. It is not added to the two-region list: the SM8750 GPU
node also describes the cx_dbgc region, which the generic three-entry
reg-names list already allows.

Assisted-by: Grok
Signed-off-by: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml
index e5efe2d35..bfa0f8952 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/gpu.yaml
@@ -451,6 +451,7 @@ allOf:
               - qcom,adreno-43050c01
               - qcom,adreno-43051401
               - qcom,adreno-44010000
+              - qcom,adreno-44050000
               - qcom,adreno-44050a01
               - qcom,adreno-44070001
 
